<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct construction orders rise 1.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct construction orders rise 1.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's construction orders in October rose 1.5 percent from a year earlier to 1.34 trillion yen, the Construction Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in billions of yen unless specified, with year-on-year changes):</p>
<p> Domestic private-sector orders		  705.75  -13.2</p>
<p> Domestic public-sector orders		   472.55  +13.3</p>
<p>Foreign government facilities in Japan and</p>
<p>    orders of less than 10 million yen	  38.08   +2.0</p>
<p> Orders received abroad			    124.60 +128.8</p>
<p> Total						1.34 trln   +1.5</p>
</text>
